-- title:
--   Existence of a resolved Deligne–Rapoport model with étale crossing charts
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. the package of data and properties attached to `DRModel p`, the two-chart integral model over $\mathbb Z$ of the curve with function field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` and coordinate the Igusa $j$-invariant (properness, flatness and integrality of `DRModel.toBase p`, normality, generic-fibre curve models over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with their Galois compatibilities, the two sections $\varepsilon_{\infty},\varepsilon_0$, the smooth locus, and the component maps `compInf`, `compZero`). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to\kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Assume that every point $x$ of the fibre product of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ (the intersection of the two components of the geometric fibre at $p$) is residually rational over $O$, in the precise sense that there is a morphism $s$ from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field of $O$ to $\mathrm{DRModel}\times_{\mathbb Z}\operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak m)$ splitting the second projection, such that the image of $x$ in $\mathrm{DRModel}\times_{\mathbb Z}\operatorname{Spec}O$ under `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` coincides with the image under `DRModel.baseChangeMap (IsLocalRing.residue O)` of the closed point's image under $s$. The conclusion asserts the existence of two things. First, a `DRResolvedModelPackage p 𝔛 O κ toκ`, namely a scheme $Y$ with morphisms $\mathrm{toBase}\colon Y\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ and $\mathrm{toDR}\colon Y\to \mathrm{DRModel}\times_{\mathbb Z}\operatorname{Spec}O$ over $\operatorname{Spec}O$, with $\mathrm{toDR}$ and $\mathrm{toBase}$ proper, $\mathrm{toBase}$ flat, $Y$ integral and locally Noetherian, all stalks at points lying over the closed fibre regular of Krull dimension at most $2$, $\mathrm{toDR}$ an isomorphism over the preimage of $\mathfrak X$'s smooth locus and over the locus where $p$ is invertible, together with a finite node set equipped with widths $\ge 1$, a bijection of nodes with the crossing points over $\kappa$, invertible ideal sheaves with integral subschemes indexed by the components of the special fibre, and the remaining axioms of that structure. Second, a family $Fc$ assigning to each $e$ and each $k\in\{0,\dots,e\}$ an ideal sheaf datum on the chain resolution $\mathrm{Resolution}\,(p)\,e$ such that, on the $i$-th standard chart $\operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[x,y]/(xy-p)\bigr)$ (the inclusion `Resolution.ι`, for $i\in\{0,\dots,e-1\}$), the pullback of $Fc\,e\,k$ is the ideal sheaf of $(y)$ if $k=i$, of $(x)$ if $k=i+1$, and the unit ideal otherwise; and such that $\mathcal Y$ admits at least one system of `DRResolvedModelCharts` for the uniformiser $p$ and the labelling $Fc$: étale charts around each node mapping to the crossing scheme $\operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[x,y]/(xy-p^{\,\mathrm{width}})\bigr)$, whose base change along the resolution identifies the preimage in $Y$ of the chart with $\mathrm{Resolution}$, matching component ideal sheaves with the labels $Fc$.
--
--   This is the existence of the minimal desingularisation of the base change to $O$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of the modular curve at level $p$, whose $A_{e-1}$ crossing singularities at the supersingular points of the fibre at $p$ are resolved into chains of rational curves, together with explicit étale charts on which the resolution is the standard toric chain and the component ideal sheaves are the standard ones. It feeds the construction of sections and Abel–Jacobi computations on the resolved model, being used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective).
